// mgeHost64 — the scene tonemap (FSL ONLY).
//
// Static semi-HDR curve, ported verbatim from XE FixedFuncEmu.fx::tonemap. Applied to the final lit
// colour BEFORE fog, so that a point-light core rolls off identically on every surface class — near
// opaque, distant statics, terrain, multi-map and alpha all reach the same curve at the same stage.
// That "same stage on every path" property is the whole reason it exists as one function.
//
//   Maps 0 -> 0, 1.0 -> 0.84, and 2.2 -> 1.0 — i.e. sun + ambient may overshoot 1.0 without
//   clipping flat, which is what "semi-HDR" means here.
//
// Hoisted 2026-08-06 from SIX byte-identical copies (opaque / statics / alpha / multimap /
// multimap_alpha / terrain .frag.fsl). They were copied deliberately rather than shared — see
// forge-deferred-lightmap.md:182, where the copies were made verbatim to unify the near/far look —
// but six independently-editable copies of the curve that is about to change is how a hue shift
// becomes unfindable. Behaviour is identical to before the hoist; this commit changes nothing that
// renders.
//
// (Older comments in statics.frag / terrain.frag pointed at "distantland.frag::tonemap" as the twin.
// That file no longer exists — distant land is drawn by statics.frag / terrain.frag now — so the
// reference is dropped rather than carried forward.)
//
// ⚠ THE `clamp(c, 0, 2.2)` IS THE HDR BLOCKER. It is not a safety clamp, it is the ceiling of the
// whole colour chain: emissive calibration needs k ~4.5 for a lantern and ~100+ for a candle, and
// above 2.2 every channel flattens together, so brightness survives and HUE does not. See
// forge-deferred-lightmap.md:343 and forge-postprocess.md. When HDR lands, this file is where it
// lands — that is why the curve is here and not inside skydome.h.fsl next to applyFog().
//
// SHADER-ONLY, like texsample.h.fsl / hizocclusion.h.fsl / aocommon.h.fsl: the host C++ must never
// see raw HLSL. Needs no SRT resources — pure maths on a colour — so include order does not matter.
// No include guard, matching every other .h.fsl here; include it exactly once per shader.

float3 tonemap(float3 c)
{
    c = clamp(c, 0.0f, 2.2f);
    c = (((0.0548303f * c - 0.189786f) * c - 0.154732f) * c + 1.12969f) * c;
    return c;
}
